    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nHi,\n\nThanks so much for neovim.\n\n\\<S-Del\\> works fine inside neovim, except when I create a terminal.\nThen I cannot see \\<S-Del\\> ever in the terminal.\nI have tried with no init config and no plugins and experimented with some tmaps and nvim_feedkeys() and nvim_input() but I cannot ever see \\<S-Del\\> in the terminal.\nI have tried wezterm, mlterm, kitty, alacritty, xterm, foot, tmux, no tmux, but no change.\n\nIn traditional vim \\<S-Del\\> is seen in the terminal ok.\n\nAnyone have any ideas or a clever work-around ?\nI'll have a go at it with Copilot now.\n\nthx,\n-m\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nnvim --clean\n:terminal\nthen inside the terminal press \\<S-Del\\> \nyou can check with showkey -a or cat -v or whichkeybind or several other ways to see what chars do or don't arrive.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThat \\<S-Del\\> makes it through and can be seen in the terminal, either for command line editing in the terminal or for use in a process running in the terminal.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1714+g7c194c9ef9\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo, vim works ok here.  Its only neovim that shows the problem.\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux and WSL Ubuntu\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nseveral different ones, latest wezterm, kitty, mlterm, xterm, alacritty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nWhatever is appropriate for the terminal used.  So wezterm for wezterm, xterm-kitty for kitty, xterm-256color for xterm, etc.\n\n### Installation\n\nbuilt it from repo source",
